# DEMON DEATH: an enemy unit that dies bursts into a small shower of violet embers that scatter, fall a little and
# go out. One burst per death, through ParticleSystem::emitPuff (GameUnitComponent::kill), which draws at most 12
# bursts a frame near the camera - hundreds of deaths a second cost no more than a dozen: so `Rate` is 0 and `Burst`
# is the burst's particle count. Keep it SMALL and SHORT: a wave that dies in a field is hundreds of these.
# Additive and bright: it reads at night, as a quick flare where the demon stood.
# Colors are linear HDR (rgb * intensity); the scene tonemaps, so bright additive values glow.
ParticleEffect DemonDeath
	Emitter Embers
		Texture Textures/Particles/spark.dds
		Rate 0
		Burst 12
		SpawnRadius 0.9
		Offset 0, 0.6, 0
		ConeAngle 130
		Speed 1.5 5.0
		Life 0.6 1.3
		Gravity 2.5
		Drag 1.8
		Turbulence 2.5 1.2 0.6
		Size 0.26 0.06
		SizeVariance 0.5
		VelocityStretch 0.04
		ColorStart 14.0, 4.0, 22.0, 1
		ColorEnd 3.5, 0.5, 7.0, 0
		Additivity 1
		FadeIn 0.02
		FadeOutStart 0.5
		SoftFade 0.1
